<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<paragraphs xml:id="para-technical-elements" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>Technical Elements</title>
    <p>
      Technical documentation often requires code snippets and mathematical formulas.
    </p>

    <p xml:id="p-code">
      <title>Code Blocks</title>
      <p>
        Here is a sample Python script:
      </p>
      <p>
        <alert>Preview (Console Output):</alert>
      </p>
      <pre>Hello, PreTeXt!</pre>
      <program language="python">
        <code>
def hello_world():
    print("Hello, PreTeXt!")

if __name__ == "__main__":
    hello_world()
        </code>
      </program>
      <p>
        :favicon: Note the glassmorphic styling applied to the code block.
      </p>
    </p>

    <p xml:id="p-math">
      <title>Mathematics</title>
      <p>
        Inline math like <m>E = mc^2</m> and display math:
      </p>
      <p>
        <alert>Preview:</alert>
      </p>
      <p>
        <md>
          \int_a^b f(x) \, dx = F(b) - F(a)
        </md>
      </p>
      <program language="xml">
        <code>
          <![CDATA[
<md>
  \int_a^b f(x) \, dx = F(b) - F(a)
</md>
          ]]>
        </code>
      </program>
    </p>

    <p xml:id="p-tables">
      <title>Tables</title>
      <p>
        Structured tabular data definition:
      </p>
      <p>
        <alert>Preview:</alert>
      </p>
      <table>
        <title>Sample Data</title>
        <tabular bottom="minor" top="minor" left="minor" right="minor">

          <col width = "75%"/>
          <col width = "25%"/>

          <row header="yes">
            <cell>Category</cell>
            <cell>Value</cell>
          </row>

          <row>
            <cell>Alpha</cell>
            <cell>100</cell>
          </row>

          <row>
             <cell>Beta</cell>
             <cell>200</cell>
           </row>
         </tabular>
      </table>
      <program language="xml">
        <code>
          <![CDATA[
<table>
  <title>Sample Data</title>
  <tabular bottom="minor" top="minor" left="minor" right="minor">

    <col width = "75%"/>
    <col width = "25%"/>

    <row header="yes">
      <cell>Category</cell>
      <cell>Value</cell>
    </row>

    <row>
      <cell>Alpha</cell>
      <cell>100</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>Beta</cell>
      <cell>200</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>
</table>
          ]]>
        </code>
      </program>
    </p>

    <p xml:id="p-prefigure-demo">
      <title>PreFigure Demo</title>
      <introduction>
        <p>
          <term>Note ID:</term> <tag>202606020002</tag> |
          <term>Tags:</term> <tag>prefigure</tag>, <tag>interactive</tag>, <tag>diagrams</tag>
        </p>
      </introduction>
      <p>
        PreFigure allows for the creation of interactive, accessible, and beautiful mathematical diagrams directly within PreTeXt.
      </p>
      <p>
        Below is a placeholder for an interactive diagram. In a live environment, this would render a dynamic SVG.
      </p>
      <figure xml:id="fig-prefigure-demo-placeholder">
        <caption>Interactive PreFigure Demonstration</caption>
        <!-- In a real scenario, a <interactive platform="prefigure"> block would go here -->
        <p>
          [Interactive PreFigure Diagram Placeholder]
        </p>
      </figure>
    </p>
</paragraphs>